with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ \\frac{4{y}^{2}}{20}-\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{20} & =\\frac{20}{20} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, $a=\\sqrt{5}$ and $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325821" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-325821" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325821" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\tan(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-89068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/D