hacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-89068" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2}=40$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ \\frac{5{y}^{2}}{40}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{40} & =\\frac{40}{40} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\sqrt{5}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325818" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-325818" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325818" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{2}\\sec(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/e2c0bc639d03c94056b07ce1cc42976b88494f312e318199cef73043bc711c74.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,$\n$y=$\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,3)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325849" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sec(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/6044a47f621612d56138893be089f48a2d2a7060c13d044086154ab7892fac38.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,1)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106617" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-106617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106617" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/e2203c195dbcd9ae474f5d00f00e81d63ec6527c0367e96a8a7520522c967265.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,-3)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f00