" "q-106615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,\\sqrt{3})$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{b} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-106615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "x=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t"] ["math" "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/20138a518801a1bac0a76303a86d6ca4b2fe289f5dae230517730f7398de3945.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,4)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=4.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{b} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\tan(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275792" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-275794" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-275794" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{y^2}{4}-\\frac{x^2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant–tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{45} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{6}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{24} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{45}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{24} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{24}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{45} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325905" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-325905" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-325905" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{y^2}{24}-\\frac{x^2}{45}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=8\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{8} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Squaring the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/state.json" "file_sha256" "c64e8f0af83179155888a6b930b1d68726436c63c175453879edc323b0dc8b16"} {"question" "q-106671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "329d1f0065d3888ba585f3ccecb0bb41ca9da343cb5d327e6a2f72c539991173"} {"question" "q-106671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_wi